# Script Execution

Pi-rat uses **Yarn** (yarn.lock present). Never use `npm` or `pnpm`.

## DO NOT run `tsc` directly

> The project uses `"composite": true` with project references. Bare `tsc -b` (or any `tsc` invocation) emits `.js`, `.d.ts`, and `.js.map` files **into the source tree**, polluting the workspace.
>
> **Always use `yarn build`.** For type-checking without emit, use the `ReadLints` tool or run a targeted `vitest` suite — do **not** run `tsc` in any form.

## Top-level scripts

```bash
yarn start:service          # backend, hot reload
yarn start:frontend         # frontend dev server, HMR
yarn build                  # build all workspaces (includes type check)
yarn create-schemas         # regenerate schemas from API types
yarn clean                  # clean dist + tsbuildinfo
yarn lint                   # ESLint
yarn format                 # Prettier write
yarn format:check           # Prettier check (no changes)
yarn test                   # Vitest unit tests
yarn test:e2e:install       # one-time install test
yarn test:e2e               # Playwright E2E
yarn bumpVersions           # interactive version bump
yarn applyVersionBumps      # apply prepared bumps
yarn dockerize              # build Docker image
```

## Workspace commands

Use `yarn workspace <name> <script>` rather than `cd` into the workspace.

```bash
# ✅
yarn workspace common create-schemas
yarn workspace service start
yarn workspace frontend build

# ❌ unnecessary cd
cd common && yarn create-schemas
```

`cd` is only acceptable when running multiple sequential commands inside one workspace (e.g. `cd e2e && yarn playwright test --grep @install`).

## Use defined scripts, not raw binaries

```bash
# ✅
yarn test
yarn lint
yarn format

# ❌ bypasses package.json scripts
vitest
eslint .
prettier --write .
```

## Build dependencies

`yarn build` orchestrates the order: `monaco-mfe` first, then `tsc -b common service frontend` (driven via the script — do not run directly), then `frontend build`. Don't try to short-circuit it.

## Production sequence

```bash
yarn lint
yarn test
yarn build
```

## CI/CD sequence

```bash
yarn install --frozen-lockfile
yarn lint
yarn format:check
yarn test
yarn build
yarn test:e2e:install
yarn test:e2e
```

## Common fixes

| Symptom | Fix |
|---|---|
| `engine 'node' incompatible` | wrong package manager — use `yarn` |
| Stale build artifacts | `yarn clean && yarn install && yarn build` |
| Workspace dependency mismatch | `yarn clean && yarn install && yarn build` |
| `.js` / `.d.ts` files appearing in source dirs | someone ran `tsc` directly — clean and rebuild |
